  "title": "Autoscopic hallucinations elicited by stimulation of periventricular nodular heterotopia (SEEG, 1 patient)",
  "description": "Stereo-EEG recordings from a single patient with drug-resistant epilepsy and a right posterior temporal periventricular nodular heterotopia (PVNH). High-frequency (43 Hz) electrical stimulation of the PVNH elicited autoscopic hallucinations, and single-pulse electrical stimulation was used to map effective connectivity. The dataset supports multi-modal connectivity analysis (effective, functional and structural) of the network underlying bodily self-consciousness disturbances, and includes a defaced T1 MRI and contact coordinates.",
  "methods_description": "SEEG was recorded at 4096 Hz with a 128-channel XLTek Quantum system using Dixi Medical depth electrodes. Bipolar stimulation was delivered with a clinical stimulator (Guideline 4000LP+, FHC). High-frequency stimulation used 43.3 Hz biphasic alternating-polarity 1 ms pulses for 5 s at 0.25-3 mA. Single-pulse stimulation used 20 pulses per trial with a 15 s inter-stimulus interval and 3 ms pulses. Data were converted from AnyWave ADES to BrainVision format without signal modification.",
